  "_comment": "Manually authored per-image, per-variant layout. Every crop and text position here was chosen by gridding/cropping that specific photo and measuring its actual negative space and product/model boundaries — nothing is computed by the renderer. `crop` is {x,y,width,height} in the ORIGINAL MASTER's pixel coordinates (a lossless sharp .extract(), never a resize/distort — width/height are always exactly 4:5). All other coordinates (textBox, supportPosition, dividerPosition, brandPosition) are in the CROPPED canvas's own coordinates (top-left of the crop = 0,0), since that crop is the actual output canvas.",
